{"title":"DyedBro Launches Neo, Its Strongest Printed Frame Protection Yet","link":"https://bikerumor.com/dyedbro-launches-neo-its-strongest-printed-frame-protection-yet/","date":1793354400000,"content":"<p><img src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DyedBro-Neo-lead-1536x1031.jpeg\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1031\" alt=\"(All photos / DyedBro)\" /></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/?s=dyedbro\">DyedBro has established itself as one of the leaders in frame protection</a>, making a range of products to keep your mountain, gravel, and <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/dyedbro-kids-frame-protectors/\">kids’ bikes looking fresh</a>. Earlier this year, the brand <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/dyedbro-launches-evo-series-for-next-level-frame-protection/\">launched its Evo series of clear frame protection</a> to shield frames from damage without disrupting the original finish. For riders who prefer bolder designs, DyedBro just launched its new Neo series, which it calls “<em>the evolution of printed frame protection</em>.”</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DRAGON-Black-MTB-2.jpeg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1047\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DRAGON-Black-MTB-2-1536x1047.jpeg\" alt=\"a downhill bike with the DyedBro Neo dragon frame kit\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DRAGON-Black-MTB-2-1536x1047.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DRAGON-Black-MTB-2-297x202.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DRAGON-Black-MTB-2-120x82.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DRAGON-Black-MTB-2-768x523.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DRAGON-Black-MTB-2-1321x900.jpeg 1321w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DRAGON-Black-MTB-2.jpeg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DRAGON-Black-MTB-4.jpeg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"989\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DRAGON-Black-MTB-4-1536x989.jpeg\" alt=\"the rear triangle of a gravel bike with the DyedBro Neo frame kit\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DRAGON-Black-MTB-4-1536x989.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DRAGON-Black-MTB-4-297x191.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DRAGON-Black-MTB-4-120x77.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DRAGON-Black-MTB-4-768x495.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DRAGON-Black-MTB-4-1398x900.jpeg 1398w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DRAGON-Black-MTB-4.jpeg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<blockquote>\n<p>“<em>We’ve re-engineered the material to give riders the ultimate balance between high-impact durability, sharp design, and a clean, custom-like fit</em>.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p>-DyedBro Team</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n\n\n<h2>DyedBro Neo Details</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>With the new Neo frame protection, DyedBro says it is building on its iconic heritage by “<em>combining signature visual graphic styles with an ultra-thin, high-flexibility vinyl formulation designed to conform seamlessly to complex frame shapes when heat-applied</em>.” According to the brand, the new 100-micron protective laminate not only bends effortlessly around intricate geometry, but delivers tough impact and scratch resistance against trail debris, gravel, and UV exposure.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-4.jpeg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1333\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-4.jpeg\" alt=\"studio image of the top tube of a gravel bike with the DyedBro Racing kit installed\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-4.jpeg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-4-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-4-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-4-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-4-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-4-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-4-720x480.jpeg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-4-1350x900.jpeg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>All of the frame protection kits in the Neo series include graphics that range from subtle to bold and in-your-face. They use eco-friendly water-based inks to print the crisp, vibrant graphics, which are shielded by the laminate from wear. Additionally, DyedBro claims that Neo has been engineered to withstand harsh sunlight, mud, and frequent washing without yellowing, discoloring, or degrading.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-3.jpeg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-3-1536x1024.jpeg\" alt=\"studio image of the fork of a gravel bike with the DyedBro Racing kit installed\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-3-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-3-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-3-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-3-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-3-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-3-720x480.jpeg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-3-1350x900.jpeg 1350w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-3.jpeg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-5.jpeg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-5-1536x1024.jpeg\" alt=\"studio image of the rear triangle of a gravel bike with the DyedBro Racing kit installed\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-5-1536x1024.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-5-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-5-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-5-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-5-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-5-720x480.jpeg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-5-1350x900.jpeg 1350w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/RACING-GRAVEL-5.jpeg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p>DyedBro makes its Neo frame protection kits for both mountain/eMTB and gravel bikes. The gravel kits weigh 46 grams and have been “<em>optimized for the narrower tubing and specific wear points of gravel bikes, offering lightweight but rugged protection against frame bags and high-frequency gravel spray</em>.” The kit includes twelve pieces in total to protect the top tube, down tube, fork legs, seat stays, and chainstays. There are currently three graphic options in the Neo gravel lineup. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/NEO-LAUREUM-Gravel-Hormigon_2.jpeg\"><img width=\"1200\" height=\"1406\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/NEO-LAUREUM-Gravel-Hormigon_2.jpeg\" alt=\"lay flat studio image of the DyedBro gravel frame kit in Laurem\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/NEO-LAUREUM-Gravel-Hormigon_2.jpeg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/NEO-LAUREUM-Gravel-Hormigon_2-256x300.jpeg 256w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/NEO-LAUREUM-Gravel-Hormigon_2-102x120.jpeg 102w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/NEO-LAUREUM-Gravel-Hormigon_2-768x900.jpeg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/NEO-RACING-Gravel-Hormigon_2.jpeg\"><img width=\"1200\" height=\"1406\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/NEO-RACING-Gravel-Hormigon_2.jpeg\" alt=\"lay flat studio image of the DyedBro gravel frame kit in racing\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/NEO-RACING-Gravel-Hormigon_2.jpeg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/NEO-RACING-Gravel-Hormigon_2-256x300.jpeg 256w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/NEO-RACING-Gravel-Hormigon_2-102x120.jpeg 102w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/NEO-RACING-Gravel-Hormigon_2-768x900.jpeg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n<figcaption>The Neo Gravel kits in Laurem (left) and Racing (right)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The mountain/eMTB kits are claimed to weigh just 48 grams and fit on most of today’s mountain bikes. According to DyedBro, they are “<em>designed with extra coverage for the larger rear triangles of modern trail, enduro, and electric bikes. It provides a heavy-duty shield against rock strikes and high-speed debris</em>.” Each MTB kit includes 8 pieces to protect the top tube, down tube, seat stays, and chainstays. There are currently 13 graphics to choose from, ranging from racing stripes and dragons to artist collabs.  </p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/SurfsUp-Black-Clear-Flat.jpeg\"><img width=\"951\" height=\"1200\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/SurfsUp-Black-Clear-Flat.jpeg\" alt=\"lay flat studio image of the DyedBro MTB frame kit in Surf's Up\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/SurfsUp-Black-Clear-Flat.jpeg 951w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/SurfsUp-Black-Clear-Flat-238x300.jpeg 238w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/SurfsUp-Black-Clear-Flat-95x120.jpeg 95w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/SurfsUp-Black-Clear-Flat-768x969.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/SurfsUp-Black-Clear-Flat-713x900.jpeg 713w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/PLANTILLA-WEB_NAGA-DRAGON-WHITE-2.jpeg\"><img width=\"1205\" height=\"1512\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/PLANTILLA-WEB_NAGA-DRAGON-WHITE-2.jpeg\" alt=\"lay flat studio image of the DyedBro MTB frame kit in Naga Dragon\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/PLANTILLA-WEB_NAGA-DRAGON-WHITE-2.jpeg 1205w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/PLANTILLA-WEB_NAGA-DRAGON-WHITE-2-239x300.jpeg 239w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/PLANTILLA-WEB_NAGA-DRAGON-WHITE-2-96x120.jpeg 96w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/PLANTILLA-WEB_NAGA-DRAGON-WHITE-2-768x964.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/PLANTILLA-WEB_NAGA-DRAGON-WHITE-2-717x900.jpeg 717w\" /></a></figure>\n<figcaption>The Neo MTB kits in Surf’s Up (left) and Naga Dragon (right)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>Pricing and Availability</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Nearly all of DyedBro’s new Neo Series frame protection kits retail for $70, with two of the gravel kits costing just a bit more at $73. They are available now directly from DyedBro at <em><a href=\"https://www.dyedbro.com/pages/neo-protection-selection\">dyedbro.com</a></em></p>\n\n\n\n<p></p>","author":"Jeremy Benson","comments":"https://bikerumor.com/dyedbro-launches-neo-its-strongest-printed-frame-protection-yet/#respond","siteTitle":"Bikerumor","siteHash":"49f427af0a926f4232eb837006841d7242e153e3afbb590f32e4b104ea3e2718","entryHash":"fc938308f3bc9d52e4cc2224a6ad9037a55b7c7757111d5e42c2bc678238cc8f","category":"Cycling"}